{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Many Device Tokens from One IP on Failed Sign-Ins",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1110\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Many Device Tokens from One IP on Failed Sign-Ins\" or \"<ip>|Okta Many Device Tokens from One IP on Failed Sign-Ins\"\n\nTen or more different device token hashes on failed authentications (INVALID_CREDENTIALS) from one client IP within the search window. Automated tooling that discards cookies between attempts creates a new device token each time.\n\nFalse positives: large shared egress IPs; tune with okta_ip_allowlist.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_multiple_device_token_hashes_for_single_user/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_multiple_device_token_hashes_for_single_user.toml",
	"GUID": "2ab0a09b-3585-510a-ba2f-1283fe48151b",
	"Labels": [
		"okta",
